  "id": "Compound::DB00139 - Gene::55214",
  "verbalization": "Succinic acid exhibits a consistent interaction with P3h2 through multiple pathways, all involving the prolyl 3-dioxygenase activity. The evidence suggests that Succinic Acid binds to P3h3 or P3h1, which in turn participate in the prolyl 3-dioxygenase activity. This activity is ultimately linked to P3h2, indicating a potential mechanistic connection between Succinic Acid and P3h2. The binding of Succinic Acid to these proteins may influence the enzymatic activity of the prolyl 3-dioxygenase, thereby affecting the production or modification of collagen-related molecules. The varying scores across the paths suggest a degree of confidence in the relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple pathways with similar functional outcomes supports the hypothesis that Succinic Acid may modulate the prolyl 3-dioxygenase activity, potentially impacting collagen synthesis or modification.",
